---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import CtaBand from '../components/CtaBand.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Equip Solutions Group | SwapLoader Hooklifts, StarMix Volumetric Plants & Parts"
  description="Independent equipment sales and parts procurement. SwapLoader hooklift hoists, StarMix volumetric concrete plants, used equipment sourcing and agriculture parts.">

  <section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap hero-inner">
      <p class="eyebrow">Independent Sales Representative</p>
      <h1>One call gets you the machine, the part, or the <em>answer</em>.</h1>
      <p>Equip Solutions Group represents SwapLoader hooklift systems and StarMix volumetric concrete plants, and sources equipment and agriculture parts that are hard to find anywhere else. No call center. No ticket number. Just Paul.</p>
      <div class="btn-row">
        <a class="btn" href="/contact/">Request a Quote</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="tel:+15157200800">Call +1 515 720 0800</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="strip">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="strip-grid">
        <div class="strip-cell">
          <div class="strip-num">50,000<span>lb</span></div>
          <div class="strip-label">Top hoist capacity</div>
        </div>
        <div class="strip-cell">
          <div class="strip-num">60<span>yd&sup3;/hr</span></div>
          <div class="strip-label">On-site concrete output</div>
        </div>
        <div class="strip-cell">
          <div class="strip-num">2</div>
          <div class="strip-label">Manufacturer lines carried</div>
        </div>
        <div class="strip-cell">
          <div class="strip-num">1</div>
          <div class="strip-label">Person you deal with</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">What I carry</p>
        <h2>Two manufacturer lines, and everything I can get my hands on</h2>
        <p class="lede">Most reps sell one line and stop there. The useful part of this job is the third column &mdash; the used unit, the discontinued casting, the tractor part with a number nobody can read anymore.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="lines">
        <article class="line-card">
          <span class="line-role">Manufacturer line</span>
          <div class="kicker">SwapLoader USA</div>
          <h3>Hooklift Hoists</h3>
          <p>One truck, unlimited bodies. Hoists from Class 4&ndash;5 light duty up to 50,000 lb, plus the new hooklift trailer for operators who want in without a full truck build.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>SL-110 through SL-520X</li>
            <li>ST-1614 hooklift trailer</li>
            <li>Subframes and accessories</li>
            <li>Government and municipal fleet</li>
          </ul>
          <a class="card-link" href="/swaploader/">See the line</a>
        </article>

        <article class="line-card">
          <span class="line-role">Manufacturer line</span>
          <div class="kicker">StarMix Industries</div>
          <h3>Volumetric Plants</h3>
          <p>Mobile plants that batch, mix and dispense on the job. Carry the materials dry, mix only what the pour needs, change the design mid-load, and haul nothing back.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Truck-mounted and trailer plants</li>
            <li>Genuine SMI parts</li>
            <li>Operator training and commissioning</li>
            <li>Se habla espa&ntilde;ol</li>
          </ul>
          <a class="card-link" href="/starmix/">See the line</a>
        </article>

        <article class="line-card">
          <span class="line-role line-role--plain">Independent</span>
          <div class="kicker">Sourcing desk</div>
          <h3>Equipment &amp; Ag Parts</h3>
          <p>Send a part number, a photo of a casting, or a description of the machine you need. I work the dealer and supplier network and come back with what it costs and how fast it lands.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Used and surplus equipment</li>
            <li>Agriculture and implement parts</li>
            <li>Obsolete and superseded numbers</li>
            <li>Freight quoted with the part</li>
          </ul>
          <a class="card-link" href="/sourcing/">How sourcing works</a>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="split">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Why an independent rep</p>
          <h2 style="font-size:var(--step-3);text-transform:uppercase;">The factory builds it. I make sure you get the right one.</h2>
          <p class="lede" style="margin-top:1rem;">Specs on a website are a starting point, not a spec'd truck. Chassis wheelbase, CA dimension, body length, hook height, PTO and pump selection, subframe, controls, upfit shop scheduling &mdash; that is where orders go wrong, and that is the part I do with you before anything gets built.</p>
          <ul class="checks" style="margin-top:1.75rem;">
            <li><strong>Application first.</strong> What you haul, how often, and on what chassis &mdash; before we talk model numbers.</li>
            <li><strong>Honest fit.</strong> If a smaller hoist or a different line does the job better, I will tell you.</li>
            <li><strong>One thread.</strong> Quote, order, build, delivery and the first parts call all go through the same person.</li>
            <li><strong>After the sale.</strong> Parts, manuals, warranty paperwork and troubleshooting do not become someone else's problem.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="ph ph--tall">Photo &mdash; Paul on a jobsite or beside a spec'd truck<br>Recommended 900&times;1200</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">Process</p>
        <h2>From first call to a unit that works</h2>
        <p>Four steps, in this order, every time. The sequence matters &mdash; skipping the first one is how people end up with a hoist that will not clear their body.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="steps">
        <div class="step">
          <span class="step-n">01</span>
          <h3>Talk it through</h3>
          <p>Application, volumes, chassis, budget and timeline. Fifteen minutes on the phone usually settles more than a week of emails.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="step">
          <span class="step-n">02</span>
          <h3>Spec the unit</h3>
          <p>Model, capacity, body length, hook height, subframe and options matched to your truck and your work &mdash; with the trade-offs named out loud.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="step">
          <span class="step-n">03</span>
          <h3>Written quote</h3>
          <p>Pricing, lead time, freight and upfit. No moving numbers. If something changes upstream, you hear it from me first.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="step">
          <span class="step-n">04</span>
          <h3>Build and back-up</h3>
          <p>Order placed, build tracked, delivery coordinated. Then parts, manuals and warranty support for as long as you run it.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--dark on-dark">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="split split--narrow">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Who I work with</p>
          <h2 style="font-size:var(--step-3);text-transform:uppercase;">Fleets, contractors and dealers</h2>
          <p class="lede" style="margin-top:1rem;">The equipment is different but the problem is the same: keeping a truck earning instead of sitting.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <ul class="checks">
            <li><strong>Roll-off and dumpster operators</strong> &mdash; adding hooklift capacity or replacing an aging cable hoist.</li>
            <li><strong>Municipal and government fleets</strong> &mdash; one chassis running plow, dump, flatbed and container bodies across the year.</li>
            <li><strong>Concrete and paving contractors</strong> &mdash; short pours, remote sites, and jobs where ready-mix waste and wait time eat the margin.</li>
            <li><strong>Farms, ranches and implement dealers</strong> &mdash; parts hunts that dead-end at the counter.</li>
            <li><strong>Equipment dealers and upfitters</strong> &mdash; a rep who answers the phone during a build, not three days later.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CtaBand
    heading="Tell me what the truck has to do"
    body="Send the application and the chassis and I will come back with a real spec and a real number. If it is a part, send the number or a photo.">
    <a class="btn" href="/contact/">Request a Quote</a>
    <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/parts/#request">Request a Part</a>
  </CtaBand>

</BaseLayout>
